From d3a07cffbc358e01d3657fefdc9abd967353f5f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:57:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winewayland: Coordinate native presenters per window

Track all graphics clients targeting one HWND and select the newest active client after its first successful present. Keep background native presenters attached below the carrier so their host WSI buffers continue receiving compositor releases, while the selected presenter owns visible stacking.

This is a focused GE-Proton adaptation of Wine-Wineland commit 13bb88cb72c8a86fad4f1c6ca1152380ceb7c89d. It preserves the existing selective child-rendering architecture and deliberately excludes direct-toplevel and Steam-overlay changes.

Source: https://github.com/nanomatters/wine-wineland/commit/13bb88cb72c8a86fad4f1c6ca1152380ceb7c89d
---
